description: Frontend components taxonomy and structure for GatekeeperHQ.
globs: "client/app/**/*.tsx, client/lib/**/*.ts"
alwaysApply: false
---

## Components structure (mandatory)

- Keep `app/` feature-first with Next.js App Router conventions.
- `(protected)/` folder for authenticated routes.
- `lib/` for utilities, API clients, auth logic.
- `types/` for TypeScript type definitions.

## File structure

```
client/
├── app/
│   ├── (protected)/
│   │   ├── dashboard/
│   │   ├── users/
│   │   ├── roles/
│   │   └── layout.tsx
│   ├── login/
│   ├── globals.css
│   ├── layout.tsx
│   └── page.tsx
├── lib/
│   ├── api/        # API client functions
│   ├── auth/       # Auth utilities
│   └── utils.ts
└── types/
    └── api.ts      # API type definitions
```

## Naming rules

- Folders: `kebab-case`.
- Files: `kebab-case.tsx` for components, `kebab-case.ts` for utilities.
- Exports: `PascalCase` for components.

## Import rules

- Prefer `@/` alias over relative paths.
- Do not introduce barrel exports unless explicitly requested.
